00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.840
Four of 26 points is what aid groups now give Gaza's peace plan. This is Omni View, episode 241. After that grade, a security deal for Greenland, a world court finding on Myanmar, and a new military agreement between the United States and Venezuela, then a completed bank bargain and a look at how an oil buyer differs from a political guarantor. One year after the United Nations Security Council endorsed a 20-point plan to end the fighting in Gaza.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:34.020
Al Jazeera reported that five aid groups put a number on how that plan is working for

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.260
people still living there.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:41.620
The Danish Refugee Council, the Norwegian Refugee Council, Oxfam, Refugees International,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.680
and Save the Children scored humanitarian access at zero and civilian protection at one point.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.740
The plan itself forbids holding territory and tells Israeli forces to pull back.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:58.620
The yellow line, the boundary Palestinians are not allowed to cross, has moved west instead.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.440
The UN office that tracks humanitarian conditions, the office for the coordination of humanitarian

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:11.920
affairs, put Israeli control at 58% when the cease fire began 13 months ago, and at 65%

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:12.260
now.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:18.220
Israel has said the share is 70%, and a UN official told the Security Council that figure

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:18.980
back in June.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:29.140
Last month that UN Office said about 2.1 million Palestinians were squeezed into 128 square kilometers, roughly 16,000 people in each one.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:37.720
A later map reading by NPR put the space at 109 square kilometers, close to 19,300 people per square kilometer.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:47.540
Agencies count at least 1,650 Palestinians killed, and 5,975 wounded since the ceasefire announced in October last year.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:53.160
This week, tanks moved west of the line in central Gaza, with new orders telling civilians

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:53.760
to leave.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.100
Sean Hughes, the world food program's country director for Palestine, said it does not

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.820
feel like a ceasefire on the ground.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.580
Nearly 70% under military control means almost nowhere to grow food.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.480
Fishing is banned and dangerous, and unemployment is over 80%.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.500
Lilou Thapa of the Danish Refugee Council called the expanding line displacement by design.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:21.460
Rami Abdu, who founded the Euro-Mediterranean Human Rights Monitor, said territory is being

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:26.620
